<v James Braly>我能给你买杯饮料吗？

00:10:31.480 --> 00:11:01.870
<v Ira Glass>Welcome to WBEZ Chicago. It's This American Life, distributed by Public Radio International. Coming up all this hour, stories of all kinds, from all over, all from the past seven days. Stay with us.
<v Ira Glass>欢迎来到芝加哥 WBEZ。这是《美国生活》，由公共广播国际发行。接下来这一小时，我们将带来各种故事，来自各处，全部发生在这过去的七天里。请继续关注。

00:11:01.870 --> 00:11:19.400
<v Ira Glass>This past Saturday, the first of the seven days that we're covering in today's show, I Skyped with Hyder Akbar-- he's in Kabul, Afghanistan-- to find out if anything was happening there that might be interesting for the radio. Hyder's been on our show a few times. He grew up in California, but his family is from Afghanistan. After college, Hyder moved there.
<v Ira Glass>上周六，我们今天报道的七天里的第一天，我和在阿富汗喀布尔的 Hyder Akbar 进行了 Skype 通话，想看看那里是否发生了什么对广播来说有趣的事情。Hyder 已经在我们的节目中出现过几次了。他在加州长大，但他的家族来自阿富汗。大学毕业后，Hyder 搬到了那里。

00:11:19.400 --> 00:11:31.350
<v Ira Glass>He said that one of the guys that he's close to, Josef, was thinking about traveling to Kunar Province. That's where he's from. This is an area that's been a Taliban stronghold in the past. It's on the border with Pakistan.
<v Ira Glass>他说他亲近的人之一，Josef，正在考虑去库纳尔省。那是他家乡。过去这里一直是一个塔利班的据点。它在与巴基斯坦的边境上。

00:11:31.350 --> 00:11:46.320
<v Ira Glass>If the Afghan government were to lose control of the country to the Taliban, it would probably start in Kunar. And that's a real possibility-- civil war, the government falling. So what's happening in Kunar right now tells us whether that is in the cards in the future.
<v Ira Glass>如果阿富汗政府失去对该国的控制，让塔利班占领，这很可能会从库纳尔开始。这是一个真实的可能性——内战，政府垮台。所以库纳尔现在发生的事情告诉我们这是否会在未来发生。

00:11:46.320 --> 00:11:59.120
<v Hyder Akbar>Let me grab Josef, who's here, who actually was trying to get my dad to let him go back home tomorrow. I can bring him in here and talk to him about what's going on.
<v Hyder Akbar>让我叫一下 Josef，他就在这儿，其实他一直在试图让我爸让他明天回家。我可以把他叫过来，谈谈发生了什么。

00:11:59.120 --> 00:12:00.000
<v Ira Glass>That seems great. Yeah, bring him in.
<v Ira Glass>那太好了。是的，带他过来。

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:03.350
<v Hyder Akbar>What are you doing when you [INAUDIBLE]? OK, just a second. Let me--
<v Hyder Akbar>你在做什么当[听不清]？好吧，稍等。让我——

00:12:03.350 --> 00:12:05.160
<v Ira Glass>So Josef shows up.
<v Ira Glass>所以 Josef 出现了。

